//~ ErrorDupName:1 "already defined"
// A submodule named like the module whose folder holds it. The parent's own name
// is bound in the parent's namespace before any submodule is drawn, so binding
// this one there is the duplicate. Neither module declares itself, so both
// halves are reported at the first line of a designated file: this one's on line
// 1 here, and the parent's on line 1 of the scenario's own file.
//
// It is also the only collision the root of this scenario can meet: the root's
// name is its folder's, which is no identifier, so no declaration can spell it.

pub fn innerFn(n i64) i64 {
  n;
}
